---
import CodeBlock from '../ui/CodeBlock.astro';
import evidence from '../../data/vgi-agent-evidence.json';
import { vgiSkillsFile } from '../../lib/vgi-agents';
const { demo } = evidence;
const selectedRun = evidence.runs.find(run => run.runId === demo.runId)!;
const minutes = (seconds: number) => `${Math.floor(seconds / 60)}m ${Math.round(seconds % 60).toString().padStart(2, '0')}s`;
const buildRuns = evidence.runs.filter(run => run.withSkill && run.case.endsWith('-build'));
const languageNames: Record<string, string> = { python: 'Python', typescript: 'TypeScript', go: 'Go', rust: 'Rust', java: 'Java', csharp: 'C#' };
---

<section id="recorded-build" class="section-container scroll-mt-32 pb-14 sm:pb-20">
  <div class="max-w-[72ch]">
    <p class="qf-eyebrow text-sun-700">Recorded build · {evidence.recordedOn}</p>
    <h2 class="mt-3 text-3xl text-soil-900">From an empty project to a passing query.</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">Claude Code built this TypeScript worker on <strong class="text-soil-900">stock DuckDB 2.0.0</strong> in <strong class="text-soil-900">{minutes(selectedRun.agentSeconds)}</strong>, including its own tests. A separate verifier then checked the generated worker in {selectedRun.verificationSeconds?.toFixed(1)} seconds. No human corrections were supplied during the run.</p>
    <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-soil-700">Earlier workers generated on Haybarn also passed on stock DuckDB with VGI from <code>query_farm</code>, without code changes. That recheck covers all six languages. <a href={vgiSkillsFile('evals/stock-duckdb.json')} class="text-link underline underline-offset-2">Inspect the DuckDB results →</a></p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-600">These are saved artifacts from that session. Expand each step to inspect the task, generated source, and actual SQL results.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-7 space-y-3" data-recorded-build>
    <details class="min-w-0 rounded-xl border border-soil-300 p-5 sm:p-6">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-soil-900">01 · The request</summary>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-[85ch] whitespace-pre-wrap text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">{demo.prompt}</p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-xs text-soil-600">Task excerpt. The session also received the installed vgi-worker skill and instructions to work in its disposable project.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="min-w-0 rounded-xl border border-soil-300 p-5 sm:p-6">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-soil-900">02 · The generated worker</summary>
      <div class="mt-5"><CodeBlock title="worker.ts · generated by Claude Code" lang="typescript" code={demo.workerSource} tryable={false} /></div>
      <details class="mt-4"><summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-medium text-link">Inspect the slugification implementation</summary><div class="mt-4"><CodeBlock title="src/slugify.ts" lang="typescript" code={demo.logicSource} tryable={false} /></div></details>
      <a href={vgiSkillsFile('examples/agent-duckdb-typescript-slugify/README.md')} class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-link underline underline-offset-2">Get the complete project and its tests →</a>
    </details>
    <details open class="min-w-0 rounded-xl border border-soil-300 p-5 sm:p-6">
      <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold text-soil-900">03 · Independent SQL verification: passed</summary>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-soil-700">DuckDB {demo.engineVersion} · known values, NULL, and 10,000 input rows</p>
      <div class="mt-5 space-y-4">{demo.checks.map(check => <CodeBlock title={`${check.name} · ${check.status}`} lang="sql" tryable={false} code={`${check.sql};\n\n-- Actual rows (JSON): ${JSON.stringify(check.rows)}`} />)}</div>
    </details>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-9">
    <h3 class="text-xl text-soil-900">The other builds count too.</h3>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-[80ch] text-sm leading-relaxed text-soil-700">Every completed build run with the skill is shown below, including the ones over five minutes. Each started with a fresh project and agent session. Dependencies used shared caches, and some runs overlapped.</p>
    <div class="mt-5 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-soil-300">
      <table class="w-full text-left text-sm" aria-label="Recorded builds with the vgi-worker skill">
        <thead class="bg-soil-100 text-soil-900"><tr><th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">Agent</th><th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">Language</th><th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">Build engine</th><th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">Agent time</th><th scope="col" class="p-4 font-semibold">SQL checks</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{buildRuns.map(run => <tr class="border-t border-soil-300 text-soil-700"><th scope="row" class="whitespace-nowrap p-4 font-medium">{run.agent === 'codex' ? 'Codex' : 'Claude Code'}</th><td class="p-4">{languageNames[run.case.replace('-build', '')]}</td><td class="p-4">{run.engine === 'duckdb' ? 'DuckDB' : 'Haybarn'}</td><td class="whitespace-nowrap p-4 font-mono">{minutes(run.agentSeconds)}</td><td class="p-4">{run.status === 'passed' ? 'Passed' : 'Failed'}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[95ch] text-xs leading-relaxed text-soil-600">Small exploratory sample on macOS ARM64, using the CLIs’ configured models. Times include the agents’ own tests; the separate verifier adds a few seconds. This is evidence that the workflow works, not a completion-time guarantee or a comparison of models. Cursor, Copilot, and OpenCode have installation checks; live agent evaluations cover Codex and Claude Code.</p>
    <a href={vgiSkillsFile('evals/RESULTS.md')} class="mt-4 inline-block text-sm text-link underline underline-offset-2">Full results, baseline runs, versions, and reproduction commands →</a>
  </div>
</section>
